### Write Data to TLS Connection

Source: https://github.com/mbed-tls/mbedtls/blob/development/docs/tls13-early-data.md

Use this function to write and send a buffer of data to a server through TLS. It handles potential partial writes by looping until all data is sent. The handshake may be completed transparently by mbedtls_ssl_write().

```c
int write_data(mbedtls_ssl_context *ssl,
               const unsigned char *data_to_write,
               size_t data_to_write_len,
               size_t *data_written)
{
    int ret;
    *data_written = 0;

    while (*data_written < data_to_write_len) {
        ret = mbedtls_ssl_write(ssl, data_to_write + *data_written,
                                data_to_write_len - *data_written);

        if (ret < 0 &&
            ret != MBEDTLS_ERR_SSL_WANT_READ &&
            ret != MBEDTLS_ERR_SSL_WANT_WRITE) {
            return ret;
        }

        *data_written += ret;
    }

    return 0;
}
```

--------------------------------

### Standard SSL Handshake Loop

Source: https://github.com/mbed-tls/mbedtls/blob/development/docs/tls13-early-data.md

This loop handles the standard SSL handshake process. It continues until the handshake is complete or an unrecoverable error occurs, excluding temporary wants for read/write.

```c
while ((int ret = mbedtls_ssl_handshake(&ssl)) != 0) {

    if (ret < 0 &&
        ret != MBEDTLS_ERR_SSL_WANT_READ &&
        ret != MBEDTLS_ERR_SSL_WANT_WRITE) {
        break;
    }
}
```

